      "claim": "In a DFS tree of a connected undirected graph, any edge (u, v) not in the tree is a back edge connecting a vertex to one of its ancestors.",
      "evidence": "Standard property of DFS in undirected graphs: no cross edges exist. Non-tree edges connect a node to an ancestor or descendant.",
