      "claim": "Given pre(u) < pre(v) for the non-tree edge (u, v), u must be an ancestor of v in T.",
      "evidence": "Since (u, v) is a back edge, one endpoint is an ancestor of the other. In preorder traversal, ancestors are visited before descendants, so the node with the smaller preorder number is the ancestor.",
      "weight": 0.25,
      "depends_on": [1]
