      "claim": "Statement III ('If w is the lowest common ancestor of u and v in T, then w = u') is true.",
      "evidence": "Since u is an ancestor of v, the set of common ancestors of u and v is exactly the set of ancestors of u (including u). The lowest (deepest) such node is u itself.",
      "weight": 0.15,
      "depends_on": [2]
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "claim": "Statement I ('post(u) < post(v)') is false.",
      "evidence": "In a postorder traversal, a node is visited after all nodes in its subtree. Since u is an ancestor of v, v is visited before u. Therefore, post(v) < post(u).",
